  "reason": "The current best config (config_021: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.7062 acc. We have strong evidence that weighted fusion and ViT-L image encoder are beneficial, but aggregation has only been tested as avgpool. With multiprofile, multiple cell profiles must be combined, and a transformer aggregation could capture inter-profile interactions that simple mean pooling discards. Config_049 changes only aggregation (avgpool→transformer) relative to config_021, cleanly isolating the effect of the aggregation mechanism while holding all other design choices at their empirically validated best values. This is the most informative exploitation step: if transformer aggregation improves performance, it identifies a new productive design axis; if not, it confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects budget toward other unexplored dimensions (e.g., scgpt encoder or singleprofile)."
}

